+# N26 conditional controller contract
+
+CPU preparation only. Science/profile commit8fd01eb is immutable; no native
+proof, episode, source integration or budget adoption is released by this file.
+The two frozen Phase B protocols and admission-clarification-v1.md are all
+SHA-bound. The last restricts predecessor admission to root-accepted valid
+N25 REJECT or REJECT_NUMERIC_FUTILITY. Promotion prioritizes N25 validation;
+active, missing, inconsistent or INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED records fail closed.
+Even a later aggregate validation rejection is outside this Dev protocol.
+
+## Independent arithmetic and evidence
+
+The reference imports only unchanged independent N25 clip/case definitions;
+it does not use production helper/projector values as its expected oracle.
+It reconstructs full16x64x128 leaves from first8xyz and the recorded full input
+stride. Supported stride triples are8192/128/1,8192/1/64 and8576/128/1. Other
+strides are rejected. The last is reconstructed with a67-row backing and
+representative offset384. Actual episode storage_offset is NOT recorded and
+NOT claimed observed. Reference equality is checked on each actual bounded
+witness; layout equivalence is not inferred from a rounded scalar summary.
+Zero nontranslation coordinates in the reference cannot affect this potential;
+the full-shape gradient and native norm still include their zero derivatives.
+
+The frozen six dyadic cases x FP32/BF16 x three layouts form36 prospective
+backend checks. Synthetic layouts are constructed after device transfer.
+The same clean tensor object passes selection, and model_output_before is its
+first8xyz, never N25's arbitrary separate before fixture. The original masked
+negative20 addition acts on the full strided tensor. Cast origins, projection,
+raw/normalized gradient, norm, operand and after values use native uint8 equality.
+Strict interior checks an independent absolute geometry reference. Exact-bound,
+coincident and saturated zero gradients remain valid. Finite nextafter and
+signed-zero corruption, wrong source/prediction, nonfinite input and horizon
+negative controls remain strict. No numerical tolerances are added.
+
+All N26 calls require their schema/source/clean/sample/no-Jacobian tags, known
+stride,384-component denominator, original4 initial+15 rollout active calls,
+phase/iteration/context identity and whole-episode compute reconciliation.
+Only the predefined first-guided11 witnesses receive independent arithmetic
+checks; later calls have scalar consistency checks. Witness fields, first-call
+slots, reset/episode identity, same16 immediately preceding origin events and
+20KiB/220KiB/16KiB caps are checked. Missing all N26 markers cannot downgrade
+the candidate into N25. The N25 control delegates to the unchanged N25 audit;
+C0/Q0 retain their prior native paths. Zero guided requires native canonical0,
+metrics absent/empty, episode compute0 and explicit terminal0 where available.
+
+## Source and worker
+
+The263-file Phase A closure is retained; only the shared runner and worker
+receive explicit new routes. Whole-file reverse edit records restore both
+exactly to8fd01eb. Unlisted functions/files cannot differ. Old N25 control
+source257 bytes are verified against commit5a65ef, and its existing report/plan/
+process proof is checked without reading tensors. Both the old N23 quality
+attempt and N25 resource proof must be settled in their respective ledgers at
+new resource and Dev admission. Neither replaces the new N26 arithmetic proof.
+
+All four arms use the original same-process main.py wrapper. C0/Q0 native audit
+is CPU; N25/N26 native arithmetic uses the assigned CUDA backend. Every worker
+still occupies only GPU7. Entire process plus audit/cleanup is charged. Receipt
+consumption in the supervisor performs JSON/hash checks and no second CUDA
+replay. UUID/boot/PID/start ticks, main argv, runtime, source, attempt, metrics
+presence and audit hashes remain bound. Original transport and cleanup code
+are unchanged; main.py stays an actual argv token for ownership checks.
+
+## Matrix, cost and failure semantics
+
+Exactly40 primary task-major0..9 x C0/Q0/N25/N26. Seeds/init-state identity come
+from the unchanged original frozen Dev plan; no protected exposure is opened.
+Full promotion requires40 valid cells, N26>=5/10 and>=all three controls,
+substantive QD/ED and complete fixed-compute/native/source/identity/cost gates.
+Only whole quadruples may trigger wins+remaining<5 numerical futility. Activity,
+clipping and zero-gradient counts are descriptive, never efficacy/validity gates.
+
+Only the unchanged sole E2 Codex-timeout classifier admits at most2 recovery
+episodes total and1 per cell. The original invalidity, unknown tokens and cost
+remain; first valid result only. No retry of valid failure, arithmetic faults,
+semantic/config faults, interrupted episodes, whole-worker timeout or failed
+recovery. The classifier's private evidence-reader wrapper is the existing
+strict zero-guided metrics-absence exception, not a transport relaxation.
+
+One tensor-only proof resource may later consume60s+40s cleanup,0 episodes/
+model/API/simulation. It writes the existing private health ledger; its seconds
+count toward cumulative100 GPUh and recovery GPU hours. It does NOT consume an
+episode recovery-attempt slot. Any reserved/failed resource permanently consumes
+this one opportunity; Dev reservation also blocks later preflight.
+
+Current caps remain494/100h and55/199/180/40/20 buckets. Any later finite cap
+change needs an exact root-authored budget record/document; none is adopted
+here. All40 primaries+2 recovery slots and protected attempt reserves must fit
+before launch. Local cap is frozen at adoption at most min(22h, actual remaining
+unprotected hours), not a promise all42 worst-case durations fit. Each dispatch
+requires full1840s local and cumulative unprotected capacity. Validation32h and
+formal12h cumulative reservations are preserved. Exhaustion closes incomplete/
+INVALID, never numerical rejection or automatic resume.
+
+Controller status/result/journal snapshots live under the N26 variant;
+attempt/native data remain under the frozen artifact root. Non-resumable launch
+requires a new external release and no prior cohort reservation/status/result.
+Postprocessing/status failures preserve the independently reconstructed accepted
+journal prefix and all costs, report disagreement and INVALID, and cannot promote.
+All validation/formal authorization flags remain false; no protected launcher.
+
+## Root-owned activation, only after later review
+
+1. Confirm N25 terminal valid rejection, integrate the exact reviewed clean
+   source, and construct predecessor-review-v1.json from result and root review
+   hash refs. No protected outcome review is needed or permitted for selection.
+2. Review current capacity and create finite budget authority plus private state
+   binding. Generate source via worker.source_record and the complete contract
+   source_paths. Build/verify source-equivalence-bridge-v1.json using the actual
+   frozen runtime and historical settled proofs. No source-embedded proof hash.
+3. Create arithmetic source review, boot-bound one-resource authority and
+   explicit arithmetic release. Only then run qd_ed_n26_backend.py --run onGPU7.
+   Failure closes the opportunity. All source must already be final, and the
+   future Dev source must be identical to this proof source.
+4. After actual strict proof PASS, create final-source-runtime review, Dev
+   adoption (exact local cap), private state binding and freeze via
+   qd_ed_n26_prepare.py --freeze --output <N26>/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json.
+5. Independently inspect40 commands and exact original managed-login transport;
+   create execution-release-v1.json. Launch qd_ed_n26_supervise.py with --plan,
+   --release and --status <N26>/execution/supervisor-status-v1.json. No Poe,
+   credential fallback, automatic resume or protected release.
+
+The separate disabled blueprint JSONs are instructions for review, never
+authority documents. All real prerequisite refs remain unresolved in CPU prep.
